{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YBQAHuQoykPPk9nZ1iix47","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 197,\n3\t \"title\": \"[Electron v44.x.x] Overlay scrollbar not working on Windows\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n44.2.0\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nWindows 10 22H2 and Windows 11 25H2\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n43.X.X\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`app.commandLine.appendSwitch('enable-features', 'OverlayScrollbar')` called before `app.whenReady()` should enable overlay scrollbars for all windows, as it did in Electron 43.x\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nAfter upgrading to Electron 44.x, all windows still render classic scrollbars.\\n\\n`app.commandLine.getSwitchValue('enable-features')` returns `OverlayScrollbar`, so the switch itself is set correctly, but it has no effect.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nYou can use an AI coding assistant and simply ask it to enable the overlay scrollbar in Electron.\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"44-x-y\",\n7\t  \"bug :beetle:\",\n8\t  \"platform/windows\"\n9\t ],\n10\t \"state\": \"open\",\n11\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n12\t \"as_of\": \"2026-09-08T02:23:48Z\",\n13\t \"replay\": true\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"